.TH OMAWORD 1 "2026" "OmaWord" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omaword \- a quiet, offline Bible reader for Omarchy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omaword
.RI [ passage ]
.br
.B omaword open
.I passage
.RB [ \-\-here ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR name ]
.br
.B omaword lookup
.RI [ text ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR name ]
.br
.B omaword quote
.IR passage ...
.RB [ \-\-plain ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR name ]
.br
.B omaword search
.IR words ...
.RB [ \-\-all " | " \-t
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-\-limit
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B omaword translations
.RB [ \-\-names ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B omaword link
.IR passage ...
.RB [ \-t
.IR name ]
.br
.B omaword import
.I file
.br
.B omaword completion
.BR bash | zsh | fish
.br
.B omaword help
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
OmaWord reads the Bible offline, with highlights, tags, Markdown notes, and a
study Desk, following the Omarchy theme. Without arguments it starts, or
brings forward the window you were reading; with a passage it opens it in a
new window.
.PP
.BR quote ,
.BR search ,
.BR translations ,
.BR link ,
.BR completion ,
and
.B help
print and exit without a window, and never move your reading place. The other
commands go to the running OmaWord, which starts if it is not running yet.
.SH PASSAGES
Full or compact references, as the passage palette reads them:
.IR "John 3:16" ,
.IR jn316 ,
.IR 1co13 ,
.IR "rev 3 14-22" ,
.I ps23
(a whole chapter),
.IR "Genesis 1:1-2:3" .
Unquoted words that make one passage together count as one
.RB ( "omaword quote john 3:16" ).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI open " passage"
Opens the passage in a new window;
.B \-\-here
opens it in the window you were reading. A translation other than that
window's switches it.
.TP
.BI lookup " \fR[\fPtext\fR]\fP"
Opens a small window on the workspace you are on, with
.I text
typed into it, if given: type a passage,
.B enter
shows it,
.B y
copies it
.RB ( "shift Y"
the plain text),
.B enter
opens it in the window you were reading, and
.B esc
closes it. Hyprland floats it. Suits a key binding.
.TP
.BI quote " passage..."
Prints each passage as OmaWord copies it: the text in quotation marks, a
number before each verse, and the reference after an em dash, a blank line
between passages.
.B \-\-plain
prints the text alone;
.B \-\-json
a JSON array with each passage's verses. Given
.BR \- ,
or no passage while input is piped in, it reads passages from standard input,
one per line.
.TP
.BI search " words..."
Searches as OmaWord does: every word in one verse, partial words included,
case ignored; a "quoted phrase" may run across verses. Words in slashes, such as
.BR '/lov(e|ed)/' ,
are a regular expression matched within one verse, case ignored unless it has a
capital letter
.RB ( \ec
ignores case,
.B \eC
keeps it). Matches print in Bible order.
.B \-\-all
searches every installed translation, the one you read first;
.BI \-\-limit " n"
prints at most
.I n
(0: all; the default is 20 on a terminal and all otherwise);
.BR \-\-color " auto|always|never"
emphasizes matched words;
.B \-\-json
prints a JSON array.
.TP
.B translations
Lists the installed translations;
.B *
marks the one you read.
.B \-\-names
prints the abbreviations alone.
.RB ( "omaword versions"
is the same.)
.TP
.BI link " passage..."
Prints an
.B omaword:
link to each passage.
.TP
.BI import " file"
Installs a translation from a USFM ZIP archive or a single USFM file.
.TP
.BI completion " shell"
Prints the completion script for
.BR bash ,
.BR zsh ,
or
.BR fish .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-translation " \fIname\fP"
The translation to use: its abbreviation (NET) or ID (engnet), in any case.
By default, the one you read.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Shows help; after a command, that command's.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Shows OmaWord's version.
.SH LINKS
.B omaword:John%203:16
and
.B omaword:jn316?translation=KJV
open the passage in the window you were reading. The desktop entry registers
the scheme, so
.BR xdg-open (1)
and browsers hand such links to OmaWord.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set,
.B search
emphasizes nothing unless asked with
.BR "\-\-color always" .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/omaword/
Translations, marks, the Desk, History, and the ribbon.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/omaword/search-index.sqlite
The search index, rebuilt whenever it is missing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 when it fails (an unknown passage or translation, no match,
nothing installed); 2 for a usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
omaword quote jn316
omaword quote ps23 \-t KJV \-\-plain | wl\-copy
omaword search '"living water"' \-\-all
omaword search '/lov(e|ed) the world/'
omaword open "Romans 8" \-\-here
xdg\-open "$(omaword link jn316)"
.fi
